$ cat -n '/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-026/openclaw/docs/tools/diffs.md'
     1	---
     2	summary: "Read-only diff viewer and file renderer for agents (optional plugin tool)"
     3	title: "Diffs"
     4	sidebarTitle: "Diffs"
     5	read_when:
     6	  - You want agents to show code or markdown edits as diffs
     7	  - You want a browser-ready viewer URL or a rendered diff file
     8	  - You need controlled, temporary diff artifacts with secure defaults
     9	---
    10	
    11	`diffs` is an optional plugin tool that turns before/after text or a unified patch into a read-only diff artifact. It also prepends short agent guidance into the system prompt and ships a companion skill for fuller instructions.
    12	
    13	Input: `before` + `after` text, or a unified `patch` (mutually exclusive).
    14	
    15	Output: a gateway viewer URL for browser presentation, a rendered PNG/PDF file path for message delivery, or both.
    16	
    17	The [Control UI](/web/control-ui) already highlights inline tool diffs and session diffs without this plugin. Install `diffs` when agents need standalone viewer links or rendered attachments for other channels.
    18	
    19	## Quick start
    20	
    21	<Steps>
    22	  <Step title="Install the plugin">
    23	    ```bash
    24	    openclaw plugins install clawhub:@openclaw/diffs
    25	    ```
    26	
    27	    Installation applies to a running Gateway automatically; otherwise it takes effect
    28	    on the next startup. See [Apply changes and inspect](/plugins/manage-plugins#apply-changes-and-inspect).
    29	
    30	    `diffs` and its language pack ship as separate packages rather than with
    31	    OpenClaw, so the install needs a scoped locator. The `clawhub:` prefix
    32	    selects the ClawHub copy of `@openclaw/diffs`. Use
    33	    `npm:@openclaw/diffs` to install from npm instead.
    34	
    35	  </Step>
    36	  <Step title="Enable the plugin">
    37	    ```json5
    38	    {
    39	      plugins: {
    40	        entries: {
    41	          diffs: {
    42	            enabled: true,
    43	          },
    44	        },
    45	      },
    46	    }
    47	    ```
    48	  </Step>
    49	  <Step title="Pick a mode">
    50	    <Tabs>
    51	      <Tab title="view">
    52	        Browser flows: agents call `diffs` with `mode: "view"` and open `details.viewerUrl` in a browser.
    53	      </Tab>
    54	      <Tab title="file">
    55	        Chat file delivery: agents call `diffs` with `mode: "file"` and send `details.filePath` with `message` using `path` or `filePath`.
    56	      </Tab>
    57	      <Tab title="both">
    58	        Combined (default): agents call `diffs` with `mode: "both"` to get both artifacts in one call.
    59	      </Tab>
    60	    </Tabs>
    61	  </Step>
    62	</Steps>
    63	
    64	## Disable built-in system guidance
    65	
    66	To keep the tool but drop the prepended system-prompt guidance, set `plugins.entries.diffs.hooks.allowPromptInjection` to `false`:
    67	
    68	```json5
    69	{
    70	  plugins: {
    71	    entries: {
    72	      diffs: {
    73	        enabled: true,
    74	        hooks: {
    75	          allowPromptInjection: false,
    76	        },
    77	      },
    78	    },
    79	  },
    80	}
    81	```
    82	
    83	This blocks the plugin's `before_prompt_build` hook while keeping the tool and skill available. To disable both guidance and the tool, disable the plugin instead.
    84	
    85	## Tool input reference
    86	
    87	All fields are optional unless noted.
    88	
    89	<ParamField path="before" type="string">
    90	  Original text. Required with `after` when `patch` is omitted.
    91	</ParamField>
    92	<ParamField path="after" type="string">
    93	  Updated text. Required with `before` when `patch` is omitted.
    94	</ParamField>
    95	<ParamField path="patch" type="string">
    96	  Unified diff text. Mutually exclusive with `before` and `after`.
    97	</ParamField>
    98	<ParamField path="path" type="string">
    99	  Display filename for before/after mode.
   100	</ParamField>
   101	<ParamField path="lang" type="string">
   102	  Language override hint for before/after mode. Unknown values and languages outside the default viewer set fall back to plain text unless the
   103	  Diffs Language Pack plugin is installed.
   104	</ParamField>
   105	<ParamField path="title" type="string">
   106	  Viewer title override.
   107	</ParamField>
   108	<ParamField path="mode" type='"view" | "file" | "both"'>
   109	  Output mode. Defaults to plugin default `defaults.mode` (`both`). Deprecated alias: `"image"` behaves identically to `"file"`.
   110	</ParamField>
   111	<ParamField path="theme" type='"light" | "dark"'>
   112	  Viewer theme. Defaults to plugin default `defaults.theme`.
   113	</ParamField>
   114	<ParamField path="layout" type='"unified" | "split"'>
   115	  Diff layout. Defaults to plugin default `defaults.layout`.
   116	</ParamField>
   117	<ParamField path="expandUnchanged" type="boolean">
   118	  Expand unchanged sections when full context is available. Per-call option only (not a plugin default key).
   119	</ParamField>
   120	<ParamField path="fileFormat" type='"png" | "pdf"'>
   121	  Rendered file format. Defaults to plugin default `defaults.fileFormat`.
   122	</ParamField>
   123	<ParamField path="fileQuality" type='"standard" | "hq" | "print"'>
   124	  Quality preset for PNG/PDF rendering.
   125	</ParamField>
   126	<ParamField path="fileScale" type="number">
   127	  Device scale override (`1`-`4`).
   128	</ParamField>
   129	<ParamField path="fileMaxWidth" type="number">
   130	  Max render width in CSS pixels (`640`-`2400`).
   131	</ParamField>
   132	<ParamField path="ttlSeconds" type="number" default="1800">
   133	  Artifact TTL in seconds for viewer and standalone file outputs. Max `21600`.
   134	</ParamField>
   135	<ParamField path="baseUrl" type="string">
   136	  Viewer URL origin override. Overrides plugin `viewerBaseUrl`. Must be `http` or `https`, no query/hash.
   137	</ParamField>
   138	
   139	<AccordionGroup>
   140	  <Accordion title="Validation and limits">
   141	    - `before`/`after`: max 512 KiB each.
   142	    - `patch`: max 2 MiB.
   143	    - `path`: max 2048 bytes.
   144	    - `lang`: max 128 bytes.
   145	    - `title`: max 1024 bytes.
   146	    - Patch complexity cap: max 128 files and 120000 total lines.
   147	    - `patch` together with `before`/`after` is rejected.
   148	    - Rendered file safety limits (PNG and PDF):
   149	      - `fileQuality: "standard"`: max 8 MP (8,000,000 rendered pixels).
   150	      - `fileQuality: "hq"`: max 14 MP.
   151	      - `fileQuality: "print"`: max 24 MP.
   152	      - PDF also caps at 50 pages.
   153	
   154	  </Accordion>
   155	</AccordionGroup>
   156	
   157	## Syntax highlighting
   158	
   159	Built-in languages:
   160	
   161	`javascript`, `typescript`, `tsx`, `jsx`, `json`, `markdown`, `yaml`, `css`, `html`, `sh`, `python`, `go`, `rust`, `java`, `c`, `cpp`, `csharp`, `php`, `sql`, `docker`, `ruby`, `swift`, `kotlin`, `r`, `dart`, `lua`, `powershell`, `xml`, and `toml`.
   162	
   163	Common aliases (`js`, `ts`, `bash`, `md`, `yml`, `c++`, `dockerfile`, `rb`, `kt`, `ps1`, etc.) normalize to those languages.
   164	
   165	Install the Diffs Language Pack plugin for more languages (Astro, Vue, Svelte, MDX, GraphQL, Terraform/HCL, Nix, Clojure, Elixir, Haskell, OCaml, Scala, Zig, Solidity, Verilog/VHDL, Fortran, MATLAB, LaTeX, Mermaid, Sass/Less/SCSS, Nginx, Apache, CSV, dotenv, INI, diff, and more):
   166	
   167	```bash
   168	openclaw plugins install clawhub:@openclaw/diffs-language-pack
   169	```
   170	
   171	Without the pack, unsupported languages still render as readable plain text. See [Diffs Language Pack plugin](/plugins/reference/diffs-language-pack) and [Shiki languages](https://shiki.style/languages) for the upstream catalog.
   172	
   173	## Output details contract
   174	
   175	All successful results include `changed`: identical before/after input returns `false` without creating an artifact. Rendered results return `true`.
   176	
   177	<AccordionGroup>
   178	  <Accordion title="Viewer fields (view and both modes)">
   179	    - `changed`
   180	    - `artifactId`
   181	    - `viewerUrl`
   182	    - `viewerPath`
   183	    - `title`
   184	    - `expiresAt`
   185	    - `inputKind`
   186	    - `fileCount`
   187	    - `mode`
   188	    - `context` (`agentId`, `sessionId`, `messageChannel`, `agentAccountId` when available)
   189	
   190	  </Accordion>
   191	  <Accordion title="File fields (file and both modes)">
   192	    - `changed`
   193	    - `artifactId`
   194	    - `expiresAt`
   195	    - `filePath`
   196	    - `path` (same value as `filePath`, for message tool compatibility)
   197	    - `fileBytes`
   198	    - `fileFormat`
   199	    - `fileQuality`
   200	    - `fileScale`
   201	    - `fileMaxWidth`
   202	
   203	  </Accordion>
   204	</AccordionGroup>
   205	
   206	| Mode     | Returns                                                                                         |
   207	| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
   208	| `"view"` | Viewer fields only.                                                                             |
   209	| `"file"` | File fields only, no viewer artifact.                                                           |
   210	| `"both"` | Viewer fields plus file fields. If file rendering fails, viewer still returns with `fileError`. |
   211	
   212	### Collapsed unchanged sections
   213	
   214	The viewer shows rows like `N unmodified lines`. Expand controls only appear when the rendered diff has expandable context data (typical for before/after input). Many unified patches omit context bodies in their hunks. The row can then appear without an expand control. That is expected, not a bug. `expandUnchanged` only applies when expandable context exists.
   215	
   216	### Multi-file navigation
   217	
   218	Patches that touch more than one file start with a changed-files summary card. The card shows:
   219	
   220	- total `+N` / `-N` counts
   221	- per-file counts
   222	- added, deleted, and renamed badges
   223	- anchor links that jump to each file
   224	
   225	Rendered PNG/PDF files keep the per-file header counts. They drop the interactive view toggles, because those are dead controls in a static file.
   226	
   227	## Plugin defaults
   228	
   229	Set plugin-wide defaults in `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json`:
   230	
   231	```json5
   232	{
   233	  plugins: {
   234	    entries: {
   235	      diffs: {
   236	        enabled: true,
   237	        config: {
   238	          defaults: {
   239	            fontFamily: "Fira Code",
   240	            fontSize: 15,
   241	            lineSpacing: 1.6,
   242	            layout: "unified",
   243	            showLineNumbers: true,
   244	            diffIndicators: "bars",
   245	            wordWrap: true,
   246	            background: true,
   247	            theme: "dark",
   248	            fileFormat: "png",
   249	            fileQuality: "standard",
   250	            fileScale: 2,
   251	            fileMaxWidth: 960,
   252	            mode: "both",
   253	            ttlSeconds: 21600,
   254	          },
   255	        },
   256	      },
   257	    },
   258	  },
   259	}
   260	```
   261	
   262	Supported `defaults` keys: `fontFamily`, `fontSize`, `lineSpacing`, `layout`, `showLineNumbers`, `diffIndicators`, `wordWrap`, `background`, `theme`, `fileFormat`, `fileQuality`, `fileScale`, `fileMaxWidth`, `mode`, `ttlSeconds`. Explicit tool call parameters override these.
   263	
   264	### Persistent viewer URL config
   265	
   266	<ParamField path="viewerBaseUrl" type="string">
   267	  Plugin-owned fallback for returned viewer links when a tool call does not pass `baseUrl`. Must be `http` or `https`, no query/hash.
   268	</ParamField>
   269	
   270	```json5
   271	{
   272	  plugins: {
   273	    entries: {
   274	      diffs: {
   275	        enabled: true,
   276	        config: {
   277	          viewerBaseUrl: "https://gateway.example.com/openclaw",
   278	        },
   279	      },
   280	    },
   281	  },
   282	}
   283	```
   284	
   285	## Security config
   286	
   287	<ParamField path="security.allowRemoteViewer" type="boolean" default="false">
   288	  `false`: non-loopback requests to viewer routes are denied. `true`: remote viewers are allowed if the tokenized path is valid.
   289	</ParamField>
   290	
   291	```json5
   292	{
   293	  plugins: {
   294	    entries: {
   295	      diffs: {
   296	        enabled: true,
   297	        config: {
   298	          security: {
   299	            allowRemoteViewer: false,
   300	          },
   301	        },
   302	      },
   303	    },
   304	  },
   305	}
   306	```
   307	
   308	## Artifact lifecycle and storage
   309	
   310	- Viewer HTML and metadata live in the shared `state/openclaw.sqlite` database under the Diffs plugin blob namespace. HTML is gzip-compressed. SQLite stores only a SHA-256 hash of the random URL token, not the token itself.
   311	- Rendered PNG/PDF files remain temporary materializations under `$TMPDIR/openclaw-diffs` because channel delivery requires a file path. SQLite owns their expiry metadata. OpenClaw writes no JSON sidecars.
   312	- Default artifact TTL: 30 minutes. Maximum accepted TTL: 6 hours.
   313	- Cleanup runs opportunistically after each artifact create call. Expired SQLite rows are deleted first, followed by any corresponding PNG/PDF directory.
   314	- A fallback sweep removes rowless temporary folders older than 24 hours. Legacy `meta.json`, `file-meta.json`, and `viewer.html` caches are not imported or read.
   315	
   316	## Viewer URL and network behavior
   317	
   318	Viewer route: `/plugins/diffs/view/{artifactId}/{token}`
   319	
   320	Viewer assets:
   321	
   322	- `/plugins/diffs/assets/viewer.js`
   323	- `/plugins/diffs/assets/viewer-runtime.js`
   324	- `/plugins/diffs-language-pack/assets/viewer.js` (only when the diff uses a language pack language)
   325	
   326	The viewer document resolves these assets relative to the viewer URL. An optional `baseUrl` path prefix therefore carries through to asset requests too.
   327	
   328	URL resolution order: tool-call `baseUrl` (after strict validation) -> plugin `viewerBaseUrl` -> `gateway.publicOrigin` -> the existing bind-aware Gateway fallback.
   329	
   330	`baseUrl` rules:
   331	
   332	- The scheme must be `http://` or `https://`.
   333	- A `baseUrl` that carries a query string or a hash is rejected.
   334	- An origin plus an optional base path is allowed.
   335	
   336	## Security model
   337	
   338	<AccordionGroup>
   339	  <Accordion title="Viewer hardening">
   340	    - Loopback-only by default.
   341	    - Tokenized viewer paths with strict ID and token pattern validation.
   342	    - Viewer response CSP: `default-src 'none'`. Scripts and assets load only from self. The viewer makes no outbound `connect-src` requests.
   343	    - Remote miss throttling when remote access is enabled: 40 failures per 60 seconds triggers a 60-second lockout (`429 Too Many Requests`).
   344	
   345	  </Accordion>
   346	  <Accordion title="File rendering hardening">
   347	    - Screenshot browser request routing is deny-by-default.
   348	    - Only local viewer assets from `http://127.0.0.1/plugins/diffs/assets/*` are allowed.
   349	    - External network requests are blocked.
   350	
   351	  </Accordion>
   352	</AccordionGroup>
   353	
   354	## Browser requirements for file mode
   355	
   356	`mode: "file"` and `mode: "both"` need a Chromium-compatible browser.
   357	
   358	Resolution order:
   359	
   360	<Steps>
   361	  <Step title="Config">
   362	    `browser.executablePath` in OpenClaw config.
   363	  </Step>
   364	  <Step title="Environment variables">
   365	    - `OPENCLAW_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH`
   366	    - `BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH`
   367	    - `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH`
   368	
   369	  </Step>
   370	  <Step title="Platform fallback">
   371	    Common install paths and `PATH` lookups for Chrome, Chromium, Edge, and Brave.
   372	  </Step>
   373	</Steps>
   374	
   375	Common failure text: `Diff PNG/PDF rendering requires a Chromium-compatible browser...`. Fix by installing Chrome, Chromium, Edge, or Brave, or setting one of the executable path options above.
   376	
   377	## Troubleshooting
   378	
   379	<AccordionGroup>
   380	  <Accordion title="Input validation errors">
   381	    - `Provide patch or both before and after text.` -- include both `before` and `after`, or provide `patch`.
   382	    - `Provide either patch or before/after input, not both.` -- do not mix input modes.
   383	    - `Invalid baseUrl: ...` -- use an `http(s)` origin with optional path, no query/hash.
   384	    - `{field} exceeds maximum size (...)` -- reduce payload size.
   385	    - Large patch rejection -- reduce patch file count or total lines.
   386	
   387	  </Accordion>
   388	  <Accordion title="Viewer accessibility">
   389	    - Viewer URL resolves to `127.0.0.1` by default.
   390	    - For remote access, set `gateway.publicOrigin`, set plugin `viewerBaseUrl`, or pass `baseUrl` per call.
   391	    - `gateway.trustedProxies` can include loopback for a same-host proxy such as Tailscale Serve. Raw loopback viewer requests without forwarded client-IP headers then fail closed by design.
   392	    - For that proxy topology, prefer `mode: "file"`/`"both"` for an attachment. For a shareable viewer link, intentionally enable `security.allowRemoteViewer` plus plugin `viewerBaseUrl`/a proxy `baseUrl`.
   393	    - Enable `security.allowRemoteViewer` only when external viewer access is intended.
   394	
   395	  </Accordion>
   396	  <Accordion title="Unmodified-lines row has no expand button">
   397	    Expected for patch input that lacks expandable context. This is not a viewer failure.
   398	  </Accordion>
   399	  <Accordion title="Artifact not found">
   400	    - Artifact expired due to TTL.
   401	    - Token or path changed.
   402	    - Cleanup removed stale data.
   403	
   404	  </Accordion>
   405	</AccordionGroup>
   406	
   407	## Operational guidance
   408	
   409	- Prefer `mode: "view"` for local interactive reviews in a browser.
   410	- Prefer `mode: "file"` for outbound chat channels that need an attachment.
   411	- Keep `allowRemoteViewer` disabled unless your deployment requires remote viewer URLs.
   412	- Set an explicit short `ttlSeconds` for sensitive diffs.
   413	- Avoid sending secrets in diff input when not required.
   414	- If your channel compresses images aggressively (for example Telegram or WhatsApp), prefer PDF output (`fileFormat: "pdf"`).
   415	
   416	<Note>
   417	Diff rendering engine powered by [Diffs](https://diffs.com).
   418	</Note>
   419	
